 The sidebar is the main Herdr dashboard. Its expanded desktop view is one session tree: workspaces contain tabs, and tabs contain shell or Agent panes. A tab with one pane is condensed into one pane row; a split tab shows an unnumbered, selectable tab row with each numbered pane beneath it. Clicking or selecting a workspace, tab, or pane focuses it. Press `prefix+w` to focus the tree from the keyboard, then use `j`/`k`, `h`/`l`, Enter, and `/` for movement, collapse/expand, activation, and inline filtering. In Navigate mode, the selected row uses the active theme accent; outside Navigate mode, the currently focused pane keeps that accent background. Search `ui.` in the [Config reference](/docs/config-reference/) for sizing, collapsed mode, mouse behavior, pane borders, and other presentation settings. `ui.agent_panel_sort` still controls Agent cycling and the compact collapsed rail; it does not reorder the hierarchical tree.
 
+Set `hide_tab_bar = true` under `[ui]` to hide the desktop tab row regardless of tab count or position. Tabs remain accessible through the sidebar and configured keybindings. This takes precedence over `hide_tab_bar_when_single_tab`, which only hides the row for a workspace with one tab. Both options default to `false`.
+
 Set `tab_bar_position = "bottom"` under `[ui]` to place the desktop tab row below the terminal panes. Prefix, Navigate, Copy, and Resize mode bars temporarily replace the bottom tab row while active. The default is `"top"`.
 
 Configure an ordered tmux-style status area at the right edge of the tab row:
